{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traversal\/directedsimplepaths"]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedSimplePaths"}],"externalID":"s:9Traversal19DirectedSimplePathsV","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SimplePaths.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Traversal\/SimplePaths.swift#L222"},"modules":[{"name":"Traversal"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedSimplePaths"}],"role":"symbol","title":"DirectedSimplePaths"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/ST"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedSimplePaths"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DirectedGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each copy of a parallel edge gives a different path. A path reaching one target continues to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the others, so a path through a target to another is listed after the shorter one. The source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"itself, when it is a target, gives the trivial path first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sequence holds the graph (a value), so iterating again gives the same paths. The first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the rows the source reaches, O(n + m). A vertex that reaches no target is never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entered, but a partial path can still end where every way on is blocked by its own vertices,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the time between two paths is not bounded by a polynomial in n + m."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Iterator"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/maxLength"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/makeIterator()"],"generated":true},{"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Element"],"generated":true},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Sequence-Implementations"],"generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every simple path of a directed graph from a source to any of a set of targets, lazily, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "}